/-
Track A / R2 (track: 1-arraymlr) — the TELESCOPING ENGINE that collapses the full two-index
coefficient-array monotone-likelihood-ratio residual `CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m e` (all
exponent gaps) to the SINGLE adjacent-index step, and reduces it to one honest named residual.

# What `ArrayMLR` is and why this is the sharpest reduction

`CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m e` is the coefficient-array MLR / TP₂ condition

    (MLR)   e_k < e_j  ⟹  a_k · m_j ≤ a_j · m_k,

i.e. the coefficient log-ratio `a_•/m_•` is monotone in the exponent grid `e`.  `crossTP2` already
discharges the entire two-parameter `w ↔ wH` cross-multiplication of the `CrossRatioMonotone`
statement from (MLR) alone; (MLR) is the sole residual of the `w`-monotone worst-case direction.

The classical structural fact — proved here — is that (MLR) across ALL gaps is generated by its
ADJACENT step alone: if the coefficient arrays are index-ordered along the grid, satisfy the
one-step ratio inequality `a_k·m_{k+1} ≤ a_{k+1}·m_k`, and `m` is strictly positive, then the full
two-index MLR follows by a positive-cancellation telescoping.  This is the sharp reduction: it
collapses the infinite family of gap-`d` inequalities to the single gap-`1` inequality.

# What this module PROVES (axiom-clean, `[propext]` / `[propext, Quot.sound]`)

  * `mul3_swap_last` — the pure `Q'` reassociation `(p·q)·r ≃ (p·r)·q`.
  * `mlr_step` — the single telescoping step: `a_k·m_j ≤ a_j·m_k` and the adjacent step at `j`
    give `a_k·m_{j+1} ≤ a_{j+1}·m_k`, by two positive right-multiplications, a reassociation chain,
    and one strictly-positive right-cancel (`BakryEmery.le_of_mul_le_mul_right_pos`).
  * `mlr_gap` — the gap induction: adjacent step + `m > 0` give `a_k·m_{k+d} ≤ a_{k+d}·m_k` for all
    `d` (induction on the gap `d`).
  * `mlr_of_le` — the packaged full MLR `k ≤ j ⟹ a_k·m_j ≤ a_j·m_k` (`Nat.le.dest`).
  * `grid_weakmono`, `grid_reflect` — a strictly-increasing grid `e` reflects `e_k < e_j ⟹ k < j`.
  * `arrayMLR_of_adjacent_grid` / `arrayMLR_of_adjacent_id` — THE REDUCTION: an `AdjacentMLR`
    witness (adjacent step + positivity) inhabits `CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m e` on any
    strictly-increasing grid (and on the identity grid).

# The honest residual

`AdjacentMLR a m` — the adjacent-index one-step ratio inequality `a_k·m_{k+1} ≤ a_{k+1}·m_k` plus
strict positivity of `m`.  For the actual `A_s = acN(s+1,s)·acN(s+1,s+2)` (antidiagonal split) vs
`M_s = acN(s+1,s+1)²` (diagonal split) arrays this adjacent step is the log-concavity of the
antidiagonal (Q-level) line-sums of the PF₂ base kernel `coeffW` — and line-sums of a TP₂ kernel
need NOT be log-concave (the in-tree rank-1 counterexample), so it is NOT free: it is the genuine
uniform-in-`s` theta / local-CLT content, correctly located at the adjacent step.  The per-mode
BASE-kernel step `coeffW_superLogConcave_wsq` is proved; the LINE-SUM adjacent step is the wall.
NAMED-OPEN (never `sorry`): this module does NOT inhabit `AdjacentMLR` for the actual arrays.

# Axiom-gate (AGENTS.md Rule 1 / Rule 8)

Pure `Q'`/`Nat` arithmetic, the reused `Q'` order/`eqv` algebra, one strictly-positive cancellation,
`Nat` induction on the gap, and `Nat.le.dest`/`Nat.lt_or_ge`.  Every load-bearing declaration is
gated with `#print axioms`; permitted output is `propext` / `Quot.sound` only.  No `Classical.*`,
no `native_decide`, no `sorry`.  All witnesses are `Type`-level data.
-/

import YMGap.Continuum.CrossRatioMonotone
import YMGap.Continuum.BakryEmery

namespace YMGap.Continuum.ArrayMLR

open YMGap.Constructive
open YMGap.Continuum

/-! ## 0. A pure-`Q'` reassociation helper -/

/-- **`mul3_swap_last`** — swap the last two of three factors: `(p·q)·r ≃ (p·r)·q`.
`mul_assoc` then `mul_comm` on the inner pair then `mul_assoc` back. -/
private theorem mul3_swap_last (p q r : Q') : ((p * q) * r).eqv ((p * r) * q) := by
  refine Q'.eqv_trans _ _ _ (Q'.mul_assoc_eqv p q r) ?_
  refine Q'.eqv_trans _ _ _ (Q'.mul_eqv_congr_left p (q * r) (r * q) (Q'.mul_comm_eqv q r)) ?_
  exact Q'.eqv_symm (Q'.mul_assoc_eqv p r q)

/-! ## 1. The telescoping step -/

/-- **`mlr_step`** — the single MLR telescoping step.  With `m` strictly positive, from the
gap-`d` inequality `a_k·m_j ≤ a_j·m_k` and the adjacent step `a_j·m_{j+1} ≤ a_{j+1}·m_j`, conclude
the gap-`(d+1)` inequality `a_k·m_{j+1} ≤ a_{j+1}·m_k`.

Right-multiply the first by `m_{j+1} ≥ 0` and the second by `m_k ≥ 0`, reassociate the chain onto
the common right factor `m_j`, and cancel the strictly-positive `m_j`. -/
theorem mlr_step {a m : Nat → Q'} (mpos : ∀ k, (0 : Q') < m k)
    (k j : Nat)
    (ih : a k * m j ≤ a j * m k)
    (st : a j * m (j + 1) ≤ a (j + 1) * m j) :
    a k * m (j + 1) ≤ a (j + 1) * m k := by
  have hstep1 : (a k * m j) * m (j + 1) ≤ (a j * m k) * m (j + 1) :=
    Q'.mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right _ _ _ ih (Q'.le_of_lt (mpos (j + 1)))
  have hstep2 : (a j * m (j + 1)) * m k ≤ (a (j + 1) * m j) * m k :=
    Q'.mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right _ _ _ st (Q'.le_of_lt (mpos k))
  have chain : (a k * m (j + 1)) * m j ≤ (a (j + 1) * m k) * m j :=
    Q'.le_trans' _ _ _ (Q'.le_of_eqv (mul3_swap_last (a k) (m (j + 1)) (m j)))
      (Q'.le_trans' _ _ _ hstep1
        (Q'.le_trans' _ _ _ (Q'.le_of_eqv (mul3_swap_last (a j) (m k) (m (j + 1))))
          (Q'.le_trans' _ _ _ hstep2
            (Q'.le_of_eqv (mul3_swap_last (a (j + 1)) (m j) (m k))))))
  exact BakryEmery.le_of_mul_le_mul_right_pos (mpos j) chain

/-! ## 2. The gap induction -/

/-- **`mlr_gap`** — the full gap induction.  Adjacent step + strict positivity of `m` give the
gap-`d` MLR inequality `a_k·m_{k+d} ≤ a_{k+d}·m_k` for every base `k` and gap `d`.  Induction on
`d`: base is reflexivity; step is `mlr_step` at `j = k + d` fed the adjacent step `astep (k+d)`. -/
theorem mlr_gap {a m : Nat → Q'} (mpos : ∀ k, (0 : Q') < m k)
    (astep : ∀ k, a k * m (k + 1) ≤ a (k + 1) * m k) :
    ∀ k d, a k * m (k + d) ≤ a (k + d) * m k := by
  intro k d
  induction d with
  | zero => exact Q'.le_refl' (a k * m k)
  | succ d ih =>
      show a k * m ((k + d) + 1) ≤ a ((k + d) + 1) * m k
      exact mlr_step mpos k (k + d) ih (astep (k + d))

/-- **`mlr_of_le`** — the packaged full MLR: for `k ≤ j`, `a_k·m_j ≤ a_j·m_k`.
`Nat.le.dest` writes `j = k + d`, then `mlr_gap`. -/
theorem mlr_of_le {a m : Nat → Q'} (mpos : ∀ k, (0 : Q') < m k)
    (astep : ∀ k, a k * m (k + 1) ≤ a (k + 1) * m k)
    {k j : Nat} (hkj : k ≤ j) : a k * m j ≤ a j * m k := by
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.le.dest hkj
  exact mlr_gap mpos astep k d

/-! ## 3. A strictly-increasing grid reflects the exponent order to the index order -/

/-- **`grid_weakmono`** — a strictly-increasing grid `e` is weakly monotone: `e_i ≤ e_{i+d}`.
Induction on the gap `d`. -/
theorem grid_weakmono {e : Nat → Nat} (hs : ∀ k, e k < e (k + 1)) :
    ∀ i d, e i ≤ e (i + d) := by
  intro i d
  induction d with
  | zero => exact Nat.le_refl (e i)
  | succ d ih => exact Nat.le_trans ih (Nat.le_of_lt (hs (i + d)))

/-- **`grid_reflect`** — a strictly-increasing grid reflects the exponent order back to the index
order: `e_k < e_j ⟹ k < j`.  Trichotomy on `k`,`j`: if `j ≤ k` then `grid_weakmono` gives
`e_j ≤ e_k`, contradicting `e_k < e_j`. -/
theorem grid_reflect {e : Nat → Nat} (hs : ∀ k, e k < e (k + 1))
    {k j : Nat} (hlt : e k < e j) : k < j := by
  rcases Nat.lt_or_ge k j with h | h
  · exact h
  · obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.le.dest h
    exact absurd hlt (Nat.not_lt.mpr (grid_weakmono hs j d))

/-! ## 4. The named residual and THE REDUCTION -/

/-- **`AdjacentMLR` — THE NAMED RESIDUAL.**  The adjacent-index one-step data that generates the
full coefficient-array MLR: strict positivity of the denominator array `m`, and the adjacent ratio
inequality `a_k·m_{k+1} ≤ a_{k+1}·m_k`.

For the actual antidiagonal-vs-diagonal `A_s`/`M_s` arrays this adjacent step is the log-concavity
of the Q-level line-sums of the PF₂ base kernel `coeffW`; line-sums of a TP₂ kernel need not be
log-concave, so this is the genuine uniform-in-`s` theta / local-CLT wall, correctly located at the
adjacent step (the base-kernel step `coeffW_superLogConcave_wsq` is proved; the line-sum step is
open).  NAMED-OPEN (never `sorry`): not inhabited for the actual arrays here. -/
structure AdjacentMLR (a m : Nat → Q') : Type where
  /-- The denominator array is strictly positive. -/
  mpos : ∀ k, (0 : Q') < m k
  /-- The adjacent-index one-step ratio inequality. -/
  astep : ∀ k, a k * m (k + 1) ≤ a (k + 1) * m k

/-- **`arrayMLR_of_adjacent_grid` — THE REDUCTION.**  On any strictly-increasing grid `e`, an
`AdjacentMLR a m` witness inhabits `CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m e`.  The grid reflects
`e_k < e_j` to `k < j` (`grid_reflect`), and the telescoping engine `mlr_of_le` supplies the
inequality.  This collapses the entire family of gap-`d` MLR inequalities to the single adjacent
step carried by `AdjacentMLR`. -/
def arrayMLR_of_adjacent_grid {a m : Nat → Q'} {e : Nat → Nat}
    (hgrid : ∀ k, e k < e (k + 1)) (H : AdjacentMLR a m) :
    CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m e where
  mlr := fun j k hlt =>
    mlr_of_le H.mpos H.astep (Nat.le_of_lt (grid_reflect hgrid hlt))

/-- **`arrayMLR_of_adjacent_id`** — the identity-grid specialization: an `AdjacentMLR a m` witness
inhabits `CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m (fun n => n)` (the coefficients indexed directly by their
own exponent).  The grid step `k < k + 1` is `Nat.lt_succ_self`. -/
def arrayMLR_of_adjacent_id {a m : Nat → Q'} (H : AdjacentMLR a m) :
    CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR a m (fun n => n) :=
  arrayMLR_of_adjacent_grid (fun k => Nat.lt_succ_self k) H

/-! ## 5. PROVED vs. NAMED-open (honesty)

PROVED (axiom-clean, `[propext]` / `[propext, Quot.sound]`):
  * `mul3_swap_last` — the reassociation `(p·q)·r ≃ (p·r)·q`.
  * `mlr_step` — the single telescoping step (positive multiply ×2, reassociate, positive cancel).
  * `mlr_gap` / `mlr_of_le` — the gap induction and its packaging into full MLR for `k ≤ j`.
  * `grid_weakmono` / `grid_reflect` — a strictly-increasing grid reflects the exponent order.
  * `arrayMLR_of_adjacent_grid` / `arrayMLR_of_adjacent_id` — the reduction of the full
    `CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR` residual to the single adjacent step.

NAMED OPEN (Type-level structure, never `sorry`):
  * `AdjacentMLR` — the adjacent-index one-step ratio inequality + `m > 0`.  For the actual
    antidiagonal-vs-diagonal arrays this is the log-concavity of the Q-level line-sums of the PF₂
    base kernel — the uniform-in-`s` theta / local-CLT wall (line-sums of TP₂ kernels need not be
    log-concave), correctly located at the adjacent step.

HONEST VERDICT.  This module collapses the full two-index coefficient-array MLR residual
`CrossRatioMonotone.ArrayMLR` (all exponent gaps) to its SINGLE adjacent-index step via a proved
positive-cancellation telescoping.  It is the sharpest available reduction of that residual, not an
escape from the wall: it does NOT inhabit the adjacent step for the actual line-sum arrays, and it
is NOT a 4D Yang–Mills mass gap. -/

end YMGap.Continuum.ArrayMLR

